<p class="docs-kicker">Integrations</p>
<h1>ContHunt skill</h1>
<p class="docs-lede">Give your coding agent a ContHunt playbook. After install, it already knows how to research short-form video with you.</p>

<h2>Install</h2>
<div class="docs-install" data-install>
    <div class="docs-install-head">
        <p class="docs-install-label">Installation</p>
        <div class="docs-install-toggle" role="tablist" aria-label="Install method">
            <button type="button" class="is-active" data-install-mode="command">Command</button>
            <button type="button" data-install-mode="prompt">Prompt</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-code is-active" data-install-panel="command">
        <button type="button" class="docs-copy" data-copy>Copy</button>
        <pre><code>npx skills add https://conthunt.app</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-code" data-install-panel="prompt">
        <button type="button" class="docs-copy" data-copy>Copy</button>
        <pre><code>Run npx skills add https://conthunt.app then use ContHunt to find viral short-form content in my niche.</code></pre>
    </div>
</div>
<p>Works in Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, Gemini CLI, Windsurf, Grok Build, and other coding agents that support skills.</p>

<h2>What this is</h2>
<p>The skill is instructions, not the product connection. Your agent reads it and then knows how to use ContHunt.</p>
<p>It tells the agent when ContHunt is the right move: any social content or research job. Viral examples, competitor videos, hooks, niches, boards, analysis, deeper research.</p>
<p>If MCP is connected, the agent uses it. If it is not, the agent should ask you to add MCP.</p>

<h2>Use it with MCP</h2>
<p>Add the skill, then connect MCP from the <a href="/docs/integrations/mcp">MCP page</a>. After that, ask it to research a niche, pull competitor examples, or break down a Short.</p>
